<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuelan M-2 falls 1.5 pct in week to Sept 20.</title>
<headline>Venezuelan M-2 falls 1.5 pct in week to Sept 20.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuelan money supply, as measured by the monetary aggregate M-2, fell 1.48 percent, or 63 billion bolivars to 4.215 trillion bolivars in the week to Sept 20, the central bank said.</p>
<p>At the beginning of 1996, M-2 was 3.530 trillion bolivars.</p>
<p>The monetary base, meanwhile, slipped 2.20 percent, or 23 billion bolivars, to 989.4 billion in the week to Sept 20.</p>
<p>-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
